{
  "id": "nicholson-bailey-parasitoids-biology",
  "name": "Nicholson-Bailey discrete host-parasitoid interaction",
  "description": "Discrete non-overlapping generations, Poisson escape probability and one parasitoid offspring per parasitized host. The coexistence equilibrium is unstable for lambda2; divergence is a model lesson, not hidden by clipping. Short horizon20 inspects initial divergence without claiming ecological realism. Illustrative parameter values, initial conditions and horizon selected for this teaching example; not fitted observations. Signed net-rate flows encode equations, not material transfer claims. No clamps or hidden state resets.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1096-3642.1935.tb01680.x",
  "reference": "Nicholson and Bailey (1935), The balance of animal populations, PartI, Proceedings of the Zoological Society of London. Classical random-search recurrence, not an ODE.",
  "category": "biology",
